BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  In ancient times, the River and the Field existed in separation. The River flowed endlessly wi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    th water but had nowhere to give its abundance. The Field stretched wide but remained parche) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    d and barren.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  One spring, the River made a choice. "I shall send forth my waters," it declared, releasing it) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    s precious flow toward the Field. As the water traveled, the Great Earth multiplied it three) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    fold, spreading it across the Field's expanse.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  The Field drank deeply and felt life surge within. Green shoots emerged, then golden grain. Th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    e Field now faced its own choice: to hoard this abundance or honor the River's gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  "The River trusted me with its essence," the Field realized. So when harvest came, the Field r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    eleased rich seeds back toward the River. These seeds nourished the riverbanks, which grew s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    trong and prevented erosion. The River's waters ran clearer and fuller than before.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  Season after season, they continued this exchange. Each giving opened the possibility for rece) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    iving. Each return honored the initial trust. And so both flourished beyond what either coul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    d achieve alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  The Oracle who witnessed this declared: "Abundance flows not from grasping, but from the coura) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    ge to give and the wisdom to return.") Tj ET
