BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each village had a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    sacred spring, but the waters flowed weakly, barely sustaining their people.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  One day, a wanderer arrived and spoke of an old magic: "If one village shares its water with t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    he other, the receiving spring will triple what it receives. But the choice to return the bl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    essing lies with the receiver alone.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  The first village, called Trust, decided to pour half their spring into vessels and carry them) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (     across the valley. As promised, when the water reached the other village's spring, it multi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    plied threefold. The second village, Hope, now faced a choice.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  Hope's elders remembered the wanderer's words: "What flows in circles grows stronger. What is ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    hoarded diminishes." Understanding that both villages would thrive through sharing, Hope ret) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    urned half of their abundance to Trust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  From that day forward, the villages took turns sharing their waters. Each act of giving was mu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    ltiplied, each act of returning strengthened the bond. The valley bloomed, and both springs ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    grew mighty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  The wanderer smiled, for the villagers had learned the secret: prosperity flows not from grasp) Tj ET
