BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (  **The Tale of the Twin Rivers**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (  In the beginning, the mountain goddess created two rivers that flowed down opposite slopes, ne) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (    ver meeting. The first river, Swift-Current, possessed five silver fish each dawn. The secon) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    d river, Deep-Pool, received none.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (  The goddess offered a sacred law: "Swift-Current may choose to send fish downstream. Whatever ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    is sent shall multiply threefold by the time it reaches Deep-Pool. Then Deep-Pool must decid) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    e what to return upstream.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  For many seasons, Swift-Current hesitated, fearing betrayal. But one dawn, inspired by faith, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    she sent three fish. They became nine in Deep-Pool's waters. Deep-Pool, moved by this trust,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (     returned five fish upstream, keeping four.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  Both rivers flourished. Swift-Current began with five, sent three, and received five back-gain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    ing three more than if she'd kept all. Deep-Pool received nine and kept four-abundance from ) Tj ET
