BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  # The Myth of the River's Gift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  In ancient times, the River God offered a bargain to two villages on opposite banks. Each day,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (     one village could pour water from their well into the river. The River God would triple it ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    and send it to the other village. Then that village could choose how much to return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  The first village, led by a woman named Thera, poured generously despite her people's fear. Th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    e water tripled and flowed across. The second village, humbled by such trust, returned more ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    than was given. Both villages prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  But one season, a new elder arose who whispered: "Why return anything? The gift is already our) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    s." That village kept everything. The next day, Thera's village sent nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  The River God watched as both wells slowly dried. Crops withered. Children cried for water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  Finally, the villages understood: the River's magic only flowed through reciprocity. Generosit) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    y created abundance, but only when trust was honored. Selfishness ended the miracle for ever) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    yone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  They began again-this time sending faithfully, returning fairly. The River tripled their gifts) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (     season after season, and both villages lived in plenty, teaching their children: *The multi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    plication of gifts requires the return of trust.*) Tj ET
