BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (  In the ancient days, two villages stood on opposite banks of a sacred river. The River Mother ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    blessed any gift cast upon her waters-whatever floated downstream arrived threefold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  The upstream village feared scarcity. "If we send grain downstream," they worried, "we will st) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    arve." So they sent nothing, and the River Mother's blessing lay dormant.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  One season, a brave soul named Briar stood at the water's edge. Despite fear, Briar placed a b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    asket of grain upon the river, watching it float toward the downstream village. The River Mo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    ther multiplied it threefold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  The downstream villagers rejoiced at the abundance-three baskets where one had been! They face) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    d a choice: keep all the plenty, or honor the trust shown them?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (  Remembering that the river flowed both ways with the tides, they sent two baskets back upstrea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    m. Briar's village celebrated the return, seeing that trust had created more than either vil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    lage had before.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  From then on, both villages understood: the river's magic required both courage to give and wi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    sdom to return. When upstream trusted and downstream honored that trust, the River Mother en) Tj ET
