BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Two Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (  In the ancient days, two rivers flowed through a parched land-the River of Giving and the Rive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (    r of Return. Each was controlled by a guardian spirit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  The Guardian of Giving possessed five sacred vessels each dawn. Whatever water she poured into) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (     the valley below would triple as it flowed downward, blessed by the mountain gods. But she ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    could choose to hold back her vessels, fearing loss.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (  The Guardian of Return received these multiplied waters. She could choose to send waters back ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    upstream-a difficult feat requiring intention and effort-or keep all for herself.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  For many seasons, the guardians were suspicious. The Giver held back, sending only drops. The ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    Returner kept everything, thinking "Why should I labor to send water upward?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  Both lands grew barren.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (  One day, the Giver trusted, pouring forth three full vessels. Fifteen vessels reached the vall) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    ey below. The Returner, moved by this faith, labored to return eight vessels upstream. Both ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    lands flourished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  They learned: the Giver's faith must come first, creating abundance from scarcity. But the Ret) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    urner's reciprocity sustains the cycle. When both understand their sacred roles, the waters ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    flow eternal, and the land prospers beyond what either could achieve alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  *Thus cooperation transforms scarcity into abundance.*) Tj ET
