BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      In ancient times, the River God offered a bargain to two villages on opposite banks. Each ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (        day, one village could pour water from their well into the river. The River God would tr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        iple it and send it to the other village. Then that village could choose how much to ret) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        urn.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      The first village, led by a woman named Thera, poured generously despite her people's fear) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        . The water tripled and flowed across. The second village, humbled by such trust, return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        ed more than was given. Both villages prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      But one season, a new elder arose who whispered: "Why return anything? The gift is already) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (         ours." That village kept everything. The next day, Thera's village sent nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      The River God watched as both wells slowly dried. Crops withered. Children cried for water) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        .) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      Finally, the villages understood: the River's magic only flowed through reciprocity. Gener) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        osity created abundance, but only when trust was honored. Selfishness ended the miracle ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        for everyone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      They began again-this time sending faithfully, returning fairly. The River tripled their g) Tj ET
