BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    # The Tale of the River and the Field) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    In ancient times, the River and the Field existed in separation. The River flowed endlessly ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      with water but had nowhere to give its abundance. The Field stretched wide but remained pa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      rched and barren.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    One spring, the River made a choice. "I shall send forth my waters," it declared, releasing ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      its precious flow toward the Field. As the water traveled, the Great Earth multiplied it t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      hreefold, spreading it across the Field's expanse.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    The Field drank deeply and felt life surge within. Green shoots emerged, then golden grain. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      The Field now faced its own choice: to hoard this abundance or honor the River's gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    "The River trusted me with its essence," the Field realized. So when harvest came, the Field) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (       released rich seeds back toward the River. These seeds nourished the riverbanks, which gr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      ew strong and prevented erosion. The River's waters ran clearer and fuller than before.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    Season after season, they continued this exchange. Each giving opened the possibility for re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ceiving. Each return honored the initial trust. And so both flourished beyond what either ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      could achieve alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    The Oracle who witnessed this declared: "Abundance flows not from grasping, but from the cou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      rage to give and the wisdom to return.") Tj ET
