BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    # The Myth of the River's Gift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    In ancient times, the River God offered a bargain to two villages on opposite banks. Each da) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      y, one village could pour water from their well into the river. The River God would triple) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (       it and send it to the other village. Then that village could choose how much to return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    The first village, led by a woman named Thera, poured generously despite her people's fear. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      The water tripled and flowed across. The second village, humbled by such trust, returned m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ore than was given. Both villages prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    But one season, a new elder arose who whispered: "Why return anything? The gift is already o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      urs." That village kept everything. The next day, Thera's village sent nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    The River God watched as both wells slowly dried. Crops withered. Children cried for water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    Finally, the villages understood: the River's magic only flowed through reciprocity. Generos) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ity created abundance, but only when trust was honored. Selfishness ended the miracle for ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      everyone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    They began again-this time sending faithfully, returning fairly. The River tripled their gif) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ts season after season, and both villages lived in plenty, teaching their children: *The m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ultiplication of gifts requires the return of trust.*) Tj ET
