BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      **The Tale of the Two Springs**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each village ha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        d a sacred spring, but the waters flowed weakly, barely sustaining their people.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      One day, a wanderer arrived and spoke of an old magic: "If one village shares its water wi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        th the other, the receiving spring will triple what it receives. But the choice to retur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        n the blessing lies with the receiver alone.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      The first village, called Trust, decided to pour half their spring into vessels and carry ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        them across the valley. As promised, when the water reached the other village's spring, ) Tj ET
