BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      # The Tale of the River Crossings) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      In the ancient days, two villages stood on opposite banks of a sacred river. The River Mot) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        her blessed any gift cast upon her waters-whatever floated downstream arrived threefold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      The upstream village feared scarcity. "If we send grain downstream," they worried, "we wil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        l starve." So they sent nothing, and the River Mother's blessing lay dormant.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      One season, a brave soul named Briar stood at the water's edge. Despite fear, Briar placed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (         a basket of grain upon the river, watching it float toward the downstream village. The ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        River Mother multiplied it threefold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      The downstream villagers rejoiced at the abundance-three baskets where one had been! They ) Tj ET
