BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each village ha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (        d a sacred spring, but the waters flowed weakly, barely sustaining their people.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      One day, a wanderer arrived and spoke of an old magic: "If one village shares its water wi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (        th the other, the receiving spring will triple what it receives. But the choice to retur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (        n the blessing lies with the receiver alone.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      The first village, called Trust, decided to pour half their spring into vessels and carry ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (        them across the valley. As promised, when the water reached the other village's spring, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        it multiplied threefold. The second village, Hope, now faced a choice.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      Hope's elders remembered the wanderer's words: "What flows in circles grows stronger. What) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (         is hoarded diminishes." Understanding that both villages would thrive through sharing, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        Hope returned half of their abundance to Trust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      From that day forward, the villages took turns sharing their waters. Each act of giving wa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        s multiplied, each act of returning strengthened the bond. The valley bloomed, and both ) Tj ET
